## Known Issues (for daylight review)
1. Unstructured.io not installed → PDFs use crude string extraction. Embeddings of small
   minimal PDFs are too similar → false-positive near-dup grouping.
   FIX: `pip install "unstructured[all-docs]"` (already declared in pyproject.toml)
2. Vision skipped on PNG fixtures (test ran with vision_provider=none for isolation).
   When you run with real images and Gemini key, expect descriptions.
3. Exact-duplicate detection via embedding similarity is fragile — the deterministic
   path is hash-based and works (file with identical hash is deduped at Scanner level
   via idempotency). The 0.9999 threshold path is belt-and-suspenders.
4. Sequential routing per file (~30s per LLM call on qwen3:8b). For larger folders,
   consider parallelism (Ollama supports it via REX_OLLAMA_PARALLEL).
5. Disk at 98% — clean up before running on large folders.

